WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.639 --> 00:00:01.707
You changed your mind on an

00:00:01.841 --> 00:00:02.007
issue.

00:00:02.375 --> 00:00:03.609
Today you called on the

00:00:03.743 --> 00:00:04.810
Pennsylvania general assembly to

00:00:04.944 --> 00:00:06.612
abolish the death penalty in

00:00:06.746 --> 00:00:07.079
Pennsylvania.

00:00:07.213 --> 00:00:07.913
Pennsylvania's last execution

00:00:08.047 --> 00:00:10.549
was carried out in 1999.

00:00:10.683 --> 00:00:12.985
In 2015 your predecessor,

00:00:13.119 --> 00:00:14.720
governor Tom Wolfe, announced a

00:00:14.854 --> 00:00:15.621
moratorium on executions.

00:00:15.755 --> 00:00:17.022
Here's a clip of you announcing

00:00:17.156 --> 00:00:18.391
this decision to change your

00:00:18.391 --> 00:00:24.430
mind on this issue this morning.

00:00:24.563 --> 00:00:25.831
&gt;&gt; Two critical truths became

00:00:25.965 --> 00:00:27.566
clear to me about capital

00:00:27.700 --> 00:00:31.003
sentencing in our commonwealth.

00:00:31.137 --> 00:00:33.372
The system is fallible, and the

00:00:33.506 --> 00:00:35.107
outcome is irreversible.

00:00:35.241 --> 00:00:38.411
I will not sign any execution

00:00:38.411 --> 00:00:40.579
warrants during my time as

00:00:40.713 --> 00:00:41.547
governor of the commonwealth --

00:00:41.680 --> 00:00:41.947
[ applause ]

00:00:42.081 --> 00:00:44.417
&gt;&gt; So you were elected as

00:00:44.417 --> 00:00:45.551
something of a law and order

00:00:45.684 --> 00:00:46.419
kind of Democrat.

00:00:46.419 --> 00:00:48.421
You got the endorsement of a lot

00:00:48.421 --> 00:00:49.488
of police unions and such.

00:00:49.622 --> 00:00:53.526
A, are you worried about this

00:00:53.659 --> 00:00:54.960
decision undermining that at

00:00:55.094 --> 00:00:55.227
all?

00:00:55.361 --> 00:00:57.129
And B, why did you change your

00:00:57.263 --> 00:00:57.430
mind?

00:00:57.563 --> 00:01:00.433
&gt;&gt; You know, Jake, this isn't

00:01:00.433 --> 00:01:01.934
about politics or any particular

00:01:02.067 --> 00:01:02.468
constituency group.

00:01:02.601 --> 00:01:05.938
This was a matter of conscience.

00:01:06.071 --> 00:01:07.139
Candidly, Jake, something I

00:01:07.273 --> 00:01:08.107
struggled with for quite some

00:01:08.441 --> 00:01:08.541
time.

00:01:08.541 --> 00:01:10.443
You know, when I ran for

00:01:10.443 --> 00:01:13.412
attorney general back in 2016, I

00:01:13.546 --> 00:01:15.114
was very outspoken that I

00:01:15.247 --> 00:01:16.549
thought the capital punishment

00:01:16.682 --> 00:01:17.349
system was just.

00:01:17.683 --> 00:01:19.618
I thought it should be reserved

00:01:19.752 --> 00:01:20.686
be for the most heinous of

00:01:20.820 --> 00:01:21.020
crimes.

00:01:21.153 --> 00:01:23.355
But I thought it was a just

00:01:23.489 --> 00:01:23.756
punishment.

00:01:23.889 --> 00:01:25.024
As time went on as attorney

00:01:25.157 --> 00:01:28.461
general and cases came across my

00:01:28.461 --> 00:01:29.595
desk, I found myself unable to

00:01:29.728 --> 00:01:31.797
ever seek the death penalty.

00:01:31.931 --> 00:01:33.299
In a private conversation I had

00:01:33.432 --> 00:01:35.601
with my then 8, 9-year-old son

00:01:35.734 --> 00:01:38.671
he asked me, you know, dad, how

00:01:38.804 --> 00:01:42.775
is it that killing someone as a

00:01:42.908 --> 00:01:43.843
punishment for them killing

00:01:43.976 --> 00:01:45.077
someone else, how is it that

00:01:45.211 --> 00:01:45.611
that's okay?

00:01:45.744 --> 00:01:47.413
And you know, Jake, I couldn't

00:01:47.546 --> 00:01:48.881
look my kid in the eye and

00:01:49.014 --> 00:01:50.115
answer that question.

00:01:50.483 --> 00:01:54.487
And then in 2018 when a murderer

00:01:54.487 --> 00:01:55.454
went into the synagogue known as

00:01:55.588 --> 00:01:56.489
tree of life --

00:01:56.489 --> 00:01:59.892
&gt;&gt; Let me interrupt you right

00:02:00.025 --> 00:02:01.327
there because I want to show the

00:02:01.460 --> 00:02:02.928
clip that I think you're about

00:02:03.062 --> 00:02:05.297
to referring to because in 2018

00:02:05.431 --> 00:02:06.632
right after that horrific tree

00:02:06.765 --> 00:02:08.968
of life synagogue shooting, the

00:02:09.101 --> 00:02:12.505
deadliest act of anti-semitism

00:02:12.505 --> 00:02:14.573
in the United States history, 11

00:02:14.707 --> 00:02:16.642
people killed, six wounded, you

00:02:16.775 --> 00:02:18.077
were attorney general and you

00:02:18.511 --> 00:02:19.512
came on the show and you told me

00:02:19.645 --> 00:02:20.813
that you wanted the death

00:02:20.946 --> 00:02:21.714
penalty for the shooter.

00:02:21.847 --> 00:02:23.382
And I confess, I've known you

00:02:23.516 --> 00:02:24.517
for a long time.

00:02:24.650 --> 00:02:25.751
I confess, I was surprised by

00:02:25.885 --> 00:02:26.185
your position.

00:02:26.519 --> 00:02:27.920
Let he me just roll that little

00:02:28.053 --> 00:02:28.521
clip.

00:02:28.521 --> 00:02:28.621
&gt;&gt; Yeah.

00:02:28.754 --> 00:02:30.523
&gt;&gt; The shooter's already facing

00:02:30.523 --> 00:02:32.525
29 federal charges, some of

00:02:32.525 --> 00:02:33.726
which could theoretically be

00:02:33.859 --> 00:02:36.061
punishable by death.

00:02:36.195 --> 00:02:38.531
Do you want the feds to seek the

00:02:38.531 --> 00:02:39.131
death penalty?

00:02:39.265 --> 00:02:39.765
&gt;&gt; I do.

00:02:39.899 --> 00:02:40.966
I think that this is an

00:02:41.100 --> 00:02:44.136
appropriate case for the feds to

00:02:44.537 --> 00:02:44.637
do that.

00:02:44.770 --> 00:02:46.071
&gt;&gt; So go ahead.

00:02:46.205 --> 00:02:48.741
I'm sorry to interrupt.

00:02:48.874 --> 00:02:50.609
&gt;&gt; Yeah, no, I'm glad you played

00:02:50.743 --> 00:02:51.443
that clip.

00:02:51.577 --> 00:02:54.146
I referenced that in my remarks

00:02:54.547 --> 00:02:55.948
today at the church in west

00:02:56.081 --> 00:02:57.449
philly where I made this

00:02:57.583 --> 00:02:57.883
announcement.

00:02:58.017 --> 00:02:58.851
It was after that and a

00:02:58.984 --> 00:02:59.818
combination of those cases

00:02:59.952 --> 00:03:02.755
coming across my desk as A.G.,

00:03:02.888 --> 00:03:05.291
my inability to look my own son

00:03:05.424 --> 00:03:07.927
in the eye and explain my

00:03:08.060 --> 00:03:10.162
position to him, and then I

00:03:10.296 --> 00:03:12.565
witnessed the courage and the

00:03:12.565 --> 00:03:15.534
grace of the families in

00:03:15.668 --> 00:03:16.569
Pittsburgh, who had a loved one

00:03:16.569 --> 00:03:17.503
killed while they worshiped, who

00:03:17.636 --> 00:03:20.873
said to me, please, please

00:03:21.006 --> 00:03:22.174
discourage them from pursuing

00:03:22.575 --> 00:03:24.209
the death penalty.

00:03:24.577 --> 00:03:26.178
If they could take that position

00:03:26.579 --> 00:03:27.513
after suffering what they did,

00:03:27.646 --> 00:03:29.815
then I certainly needed to

00:03:29.949 --> 00:03:30.683
rethink my position.

00:03:30.816 --> 00:03:31.183
And I did.

00:03:31.317 --> 00:03:32.618
I spent a lot of time

00:03:32.751 --> 00:03:33.018
rethinking.

00:03:33.152 --> 00:03:34.253
I know a lot of times in

00:03:34.587 --> 00:03:36.589
politics we get criticized for

00:03:36.655 --> 00:03:38.624
thinking -- rethinking

00:03:38.757 --> 00:03:40.926
positions, maybe changing our

00:03:41.060 --> 00:03:41.226
views.

00:03:41.360 --> 00:03:41.927
But I must say, it ultimately

00:03:42.061 --> 00:03:43.295
came down to what I said in that

00:03:43.429 --> 00:03:44.830
clip you showed before.

00:03:44.964 --> 00:03:46.966
Our system is fallible, and the

00:03:47.099 --> 00:03:48.801
outcome is irreversible.

00:03:48.934 --> 00:03:51.704
And I just fundamentally could

00:03:51.837 --> 00:03:55.007
not justify as governor of the

00:03:55.140 --> 00:03:55.874
commonwealth of Pennsylvania

00:03:56.008 --> 00:03:57.743
that we'd be in the business of

00:03:57.876 --> 00:03:58.677
putting people to death.

00:03:58.811 --> 00:04:01.046
It really was a journey for me,

00:04:01.180 --> 00:04:02.615
in many ways a spiritual

00:04:02.615 --> 00:04:03.649
journey, one inspired by the

00:04:03.782 --> 00:04:06.151
good people in Pittsburgh, by

00:04:06.285 --> 00:04:08.621
folks I've met along the way, by

00:04:08.621 --> 00:04:10.222
my own son challenging he me on

00:04:10.623 --> 00:04:13.092
a position that I honestly held

00:04:13.225 --> 00:04:14.093
for many years and realizing

00:04:14.226 --> 00:04:15.728
that it was not really a just

00:04:15.861 --> 00:04:16.095
position.

00:04:16.228 --> 00:04:17.963
I must say, Jake, I didn't stand

00:04:18.097 --> 00:04:21.967
up in that church today and call

00:04:22.101 --> 00:04:24.637
on the legislature to fix our

00:04:24.703 --> 00:04:25.671
capital punishment system.

00:04:25.904 --> 00:04:28.273
I think it is not fixable.

00:04:28.641 --> 00:04:29.942
Instead I asked them

00:04:30.075 --> 00:04:32.277
respectfully to come to the

00:04:32.645 --> 00:04:35.714
table, Republican and Democrat

00:04:35.848 --> 00:04:37.349
and join me in passing a law in

00:04:37.483 --> 00:04:38.817
Pennsylvania to abolish the

00:04:38.951 --> 00:04:39.251
death penalty.

00:04:39.385 --> 00:04:40.319
And that is where I stand and

00:04:40.653 --> 00:04:41.387
that is what I believe in, and

00:04:41.520 --> 00:04:43.889
that to me is a matter of

00:04:44.023 --> 00:04:44.657
conscience and morality.

00:04:44.723 --> 00:04:46.025
&gt;&gt; It's two different things,

00:04:46.158 --> 00:04:46.659
though, right?

00:04:46.692 --> 00:04:49.428
One is the idea, the fallibility

00:04:49.561 --> 00:04:50.663
of the system, which you don't

00:04:50.663 --> 00:04:52.665
have to convince me of, that --

00:04:52.698 --> 00:04:55.801
I mean, I just don't believe

00:04:55.934 --> 00:04:57.436
that we've never as a country

00:04:57.569 --> 00:04:59.004
put an innocent person to death.

00:04:59.138 --> 00:05:00.806
I just don't believe it.

00:05:00.939 --> 00:05:02.074
Just knowing how often innocent

00:05:02.207 --> 00:05:03.609
people go to prison and are

00:05:03.742 --> 00:05:05.577
later freed because of the

00:05:05.711 --> 00:05:07.846
innocence project and on and on.

00:05:07.980 --> 00:05:09.148
But you're also saying like even

00:05:09.281 --> 00:05:10.683
if there was a way to guarantee

00:05:10.716 --> 00:05:12.685
that every single person who

00:05:12.685 --> 00:05:14.319
faced capital punishment was in

00:05:14.687 --> 00:05:16.689
fact guilty undeniably, which is

00:05:16.755 --> 00:05:19.358
of course impossible, but you're

00:05:19.491 --> 00:05:20.826
also saying you still don't

00:05:20.959 --> 00:05:24.697
believe in it.

00:05:24.697 --> 00:05:25.531
&gt;&gt; That's exactly right.

00:05:25.664 --> 00:05:26.999
I think to me it comes down to

00:05:27.132 --> 00:05:28.367
an issue of morality and the

00:05:28.701 --> 00:05:29.468
fundamental belief that our

00:05:29.601 --> 00:05:30.235
commonwealth should not be in

00:05:30.369 --> 00:05:31.603
the business of putting people

00:05:31.737 --> 00:05:32.071
to death.

00:05:32.204 --> 00:05:34.807
And listen, Jake, I'm someone as

00:05:34.940 --> 00:05:36.709
attorney general who has put

00:05:36.709 --> 00:05:37.643
people behind bars for the rest

00:05:37.776 --> 00:05:39.611
of their lives.

00:05:39.912 --> 00:05:41.313
I believe in stiff sentences.

00:05:41.447 --> 00:05:43.449
I believe in making sure that

00:05:43.582 --> 00:05:44.850
victims' interests are heard in

00:05:44.983 --> 00:05:47.419
a courtroom and at sentencing.

00:05:47.586 --> 00:05:49.354
I believe in making sure we take

00:05:49.488 --> 00:05:50.255
dangerous people off the

00:05:50.389 --> 00:05:50.723
streets.

00:05:50.723 --> 00:05:53.425
I'll take a back seat to no one

00:05:53.559 --> 00:05:53.959
on that.

00:05:54.093 --> 00:05:54.993
I just don't believe that the

00:05:55.127 --> 00:05:55.728
commonwealth should be putting

00:05:55.861 --> 00:05:56.729
people to death.

00:05:56.729 --> 00:05:57.596
&gt;&gt; One last question.

00:05:57.730 --> 00:05:59.732
You and I went to the same high

00:05:59.865 --> 00:06:02.101
school, a conservative jewish

00:06:02.234 --> 00:06:03.702
day school -- I'm older than

00:06:03.836 --> 00:06:07.106
you, so we're not classmates.

00:06:07.239 --> 00:06:08.741
But the death penalty's fine

00:06:08.874 --> 00:06:11.577
according to the old testament.

00:06:11.710 --> 00:06:12.778
There's no problem with the

00:06:12.911 --> 00:06:14.213
death penalty in judaism.

00:06:14.346 --> 00:06:15.814
You talk about your faith a lot.

00:06:15.948 --> 00:06:18.417
You talk about being an

00:06:18.751 --> 00:06:20.185
observant Jew a lot.

00:06:20.319 --> 00:06:21.920
What you're doing right now, I

00:06:22.054 --> 00:06:27.659
wouldn't call it contrary to

00:06:27.793 --> 00:06:28.761
scripture but it's not exactly

00:06:28.894 --> 00:06:32.131
what we're taught in the bible.

00:06:32.264 --> 00:06:32.865
&gt;&gt; Yeah.

00:06:32.998 --> 00:06:35.801
It's interesting you raise that.

00:06:35.934 --> 00:06:37.369
In many cases I reflect on my

00:06:37.503 --> 00:06:37.669
faith.

00:06:37.803 --> 00:06:39.304
Not so much on individual cases,

00:06:39.438 --> 00:06:41.673
but really on something that

00:06:41.807 --> 00:06:42.441
drives me into service.

00:06:42.775 --> 00:06:44.777
And in fact, I reflected on my

00:06:44.777 --> 00:06:46.779
jewish faith when I was at a

00:06:46.779 --> 00:06:48.347
jesuit law school at Georgetown

00:06:48.781 --> 00:06:50.849
law school and wrote a paper

00:06:50.983 --> 00:06:54.787
about the death penalty and

00:06:54.787 --> 00:06:57.956
actually drew on jewish law to

00:06:58.090 --> 00:06:58.791
talk about how there were

00:06:58.791 --> 00:06:59.992
instances where capital

00:07:00.125 --> 00:07:02.127
punishment could be carried out.

00:07:02.261 --> 00:07:04.163
It required a certain number of

00:07:04.296 --> 00:07:06.131
direct eyewitnesses and a very

00:07:06.265 --> 00:07:07.166
high evidentiary standard but it

00:07:07.299 --> 00:07:08.233
was still allowed.

00:07:08.467 --> 00:07:10.335
I thought about that when I

00:07:10.469 --> 00:07:11.170
contemplated my position on this

00:07:11.303 --> 00:07:13.138
as I entered public service, and

00:07:13.272 --> 00:07:15.574
I guess perhaps it did drive my

00:07:15.707 --> 00:07:16.809
position early on.

00:07:16.842 --> 00:07:18.811
But as I evolved on this, as I

00:07:18.944 --> 00:07:20.813
thought about it more, as I

00:07:20.813 --> 00:07:22.281
reflected on my own conscience,

00:07:22.414 --> 00:07:26.084
maybe not the literal writings

00:07:26.218 --> 00:07:27.386
in our faith, I just found

00:07:27.519 --> 00:07:28.821
myself in this position that I

00:07:28.821 --> 00:07:31.089
announced today where I could

00:07:31.223 --> 00:07:32.825
not in good conscience as the

00:07:32.891 --> 00:07:33.458
governor of the commonwealth

00:07:33.592 --> 00:07:35.694
ever sign an execution warrant

00:07:35.828 --> 00:07:38.497
and instead I'll be signing

00:07:38.831 --> 00:07:38.864
reprieves.

00:07:38.997 --> 00:07:40.833
&gt;&gt; And you also know that

00:07:40.933 --> 00:07:44.069
eyewitness testimony is pretty

00:07:44.203 --> 00:07:45.838
much garbage quite often, as you

00:07:45.971 --> 00:07:46.939
have risen through the ladder

00:07:47.072 --> 00:07:48.006
from law school.

00:07:48.140 --> 00:07:48.841
Not always but often.

